Z||000000||Brandon86SE||09-19-2001||07:27 PM||||As is my Temp, Oil Pressure, and Voltmeter gauges are all not working.  Since this is the case I was considering putting in a 3-way set of gauges in the center console where my oil pressure and voltmeter gauges are right now.  I measured the size out to be 8.5" by 2.75".  This is more than enough room for most of these aftermarket gauges.  I'm just wondering if anyone has done this before, and if so did you run into any complications?<P>I expect it to be fairly easy, the only thing that really needs to be done is run the wiring from behind the dash to the center console for the temp gauge.  I'm also going to be putting in new sending units (since none of these gauges are working right now)<P>Anyone with comments, let me know.<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||09-19-2001||07:34 PM||||I've seen pics of that somewhere...maybe in the Fiero Gallery(above)?  Looks ok... Would be better if your Speedo and Tach matched.<P>Why don't the guages work?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brandon86SE||09-19-2001||07:41 PM||||Ya, I'm trying to find some that look as close to my tach/ speedo as I can.  And whatever it is that I get, it will have to be orange backlit to match.  And ya, there was a pic in the gallery, thanks!<P>As for why they don't work..... beats me, so I'm replacing them!  The oil pressure hasn't worked since I first bought it (2 years ago).  It bounces around (especially with music turned up).  The temp gauge went last summer.  It was a hot day, and when I started the car after golfing (left in the parking lot for about 6 hours) the dial went straight up to the pin!  Scared me for a bit, then I realized that it's just shot.  Now it's either up there, or at some point on the gauge (stationary).  The voltmeter kinda bounces like the oil pressure does.  This started happening around Christmas time.  I just want them all working, and my friend suggested this (and something else I'll show when it's done).<P>Brandon||||reg||1
