Z||000004||Joe Torma||09-20-2001||12:04 PM||||Is your car a stick?  The temp guage "runs a check" on itself when you are starting the car.  when the engine turns over the needle pegs high.  Maybe you have a bad ground.. sometimes the terminals corrode too.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||09-20-2001||03:29 PM||||Yeah, that temp gauge checks itself alright.  It's not supposed to... that's supposed to be the temp light coming on to check the bulb, but some numbnut screwed up and that's how they came from the factory.  Don't worry about it being a flaw with your car - that's as it was delivered from GM.||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||09-20-2001||03:34 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstmonitor.jpg"> <P>i had 3 2 1/8th guages.. i ditched the volt and air fuel for the oil pressure, and air-fuel, injector duty cycle monitor.  no complications.. but DON"T grab the black part of the stock oil pressure sending unit when you go to change it.. you'll just break it.. us the 17mm nut on the base of it. (pillar mount is voltage and nitrous pressure)<P>------------------<BR>12.920@109mph... "thats all I have to say about that"||||reg||1
Z||000007||Brandon86SE||09-20-2001||04:12 PM||||alright, thanks for the suggestions here guys, and the warning with the oil pressure gauge.  I'm still gonna go ahead and replace them though.  I found a nice, chrome, 3 dial set for $50CDN.  I think it'll look good there, and they'll all work, since I'll be able to fix anything I see wrong once it's all ripped apart.  I'll be sure to post pics once I'm done.<P>I'm keeping one thing I'm doing with this project secret right now, you'll see it when I post the pics.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Brandon||||reg||1
